From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:44:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: Clamp the off-channel TX wait time to the driver limit

offchannel_send_action() limits the wait time to max_remain_on_chan
only when it requests a remain-on-channel operation. With
WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_OFFCHANNEL_TX, it passes the wait time to
wpa_drv_send_action() unchanged. cfg80211 refuses a frame whose wait
time is longer than the maximum remain-on-channel duration of the driver
with -EINVAL (nl80211_tx_mgmt()). wpas_dpp_chirp_start() sends each
Presence Announcement with a wait time of 2000 ms. On a driver with a
smaller maximum, such as a mac80211_hwsim radio with channel contexts
(1000 ms), no chirp goes out, and the Configurator cannot find the
Enrollee. The PKEX Exchange Request retransmission after a push button
start has the same problem, since wpas_dpp_pb_pkex_init() sets the
retransmission wait time to 2000 ms.

Clamp the wait time on the driver TX path as well, so that every caller
gets the same limit.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/wpa_supplicant/offchannel.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/offchannel.c
@@ -245,7 +245,8 @@ void offchannel_send_action_tx_status(
  * @bssid: Action frame BSSID
  * @buf: Frame to transmit starting from the Category field
  * @len: Length of @buf in bytes
- * @wait_time: Wait time for response in milliseconds
+ * @wait_time: Wait time for response in milliseconds, limited to the maximum
+ *	remain-on-channel duration of the driver
  * @tx_cb: Callback function for indicating TX status or %NULL for no callback
  * @no_cck: Whether CCK rates are to be disallowed for TX rate selection
  * Returns: 0 on success or -1 on failure
@@ -309,6 +310,8 @@ int offchannel_send_action(struct wpa_su
 		int ret;
 
 		iface = wpas_get_tx_interface(wpa_s, src);
+		if (wait_time > wpa_s->max_remain_on_chan)
+			wait_time = wpa_s->max_remain_on_chan;
 		wpa_s->action_tx_wait_time = wait_time;
 		if (wait_time)
 			wpa_s->action_tx_wait_time_used = 1;
